# Camouflage replaces Bot2's declaration of blockers: Bot2 puts Hipparion and Grizzly Bears in the one pile, which goes to
# the one attacker, Kalonian Tusker (power 3), and "each creature in a pile that can block the creature that pile is
# assigned to does so". Hipparion can block the Tusker only by paying {1} as blockers are declared (CR 509.1d-f), and
# nothing here declares or pays; a player is never required to pay a cost to block (CR 509.1c). So only the Bears block,
# and die to the Tusker's 3; Hipparion is untouched, though Bot2 has an untapped Plains it could have paid with.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Kalonian Tusker
Camouflage
Forest
Island
Island
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Hipparion
Grizzly Bears
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Kalonian Tusker.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Hipparion.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Grizzly Bears.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Attack(Kalonian Tusker > Bot2)
Bot1.Hand.Camouflage.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Choose(Hipparion; Grizzly Bears)
? Combat.Blocks = Grizzly Bears > Kalonian Tusker
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Battlefield.Grizzly Bears = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Hipparion.Damage = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Tapped = false
